<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kliptown</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kliptown is one of the oldest residential districts of Soweto, south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannesburg">Johannesburg</a>. On 25–26 June 1955 it hosted the Congress of the People, where the ANC and its allies in the Congress Alliance adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freedom-charter">Freedom Charter</a> before police broke up the meeting. The site is now Walter Sisulu Square, with a monument to the Charter.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kliptown.jpg" alt="Kliptown" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: S. Honorine VOA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kliptown_is_one_of_the_most_destitute_areas_of_the_large_Soweto_township,_South_Africa,_November_2012._(S._Honorine_VOA).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
